# 301 redirects from the old WordPress URLs.
#
# The full old URL list was captured from the previous site's REST API before
# rebuild. The form and download pages in particular have real inbound links, so
# these must not be dropped.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>

# --- Application forms ---------------------------------------------------
# All four currently land on the forms hub. Point each at its own hosted form
# once the platform is chosen.
/j-l-credit-application      /forms/  301
/j-l-claim-form              /forms/  301
/j-l-driver-application      /forms/  301
/j-l-employment-application  /forms/  301
/submit-forms                /forms/  301

# --- Document downloads --------------------------------------------------
# Straight to the PDF: these were previously wrapped in a Google Docs viewer
# iframe served over http://.
/download-bill-of-lading               /forms/bill-of-lading.pdf                                 301
/download-circular-rules               /forms/circular-rules.pdf                                 301
/download-hazmat-auth-cert             /forms/hazmat-authorization-certificate.pdf               301
/download-interstate-commerce-cert     /forms/interstate-commerce-authorization-certificate.pdf  301
/download-points-list                  /forms/points-list.pdf                                    301

# --- Gravity Forms helper pages ------------------------------------------
# These existed only to feed form confirmation messages and have no standalone
# equivalent.
/credit-ap-text       /forms/  301
/employee-app-text    /forms/  301
/drivers-qual-text    /forms/  301
/empl-app-for-office-use-only  /forms/  301

# --- Password-protected page ---------------------------------------------
# The old slug carried WordPress's "-2" duplicate suffix.
/do-i-work-2  /do-i-work  301

# --- Old single-page anchors ---------------------------------------------
# The previous site was one page with anchor navigation. Anchors are not sent to
# the server, so these cannot be redirected server-side; they are listed for the
# record. Anyone landing on / with a stale #anchor simply sees the home page.
#   /#about      -> /about
#   /#who-we-are -> /who-we-are
#   /#our-team   -> /team
#   /#forms      -> /forms
#   /#contact    -> /contact

# --- Compromise cleanup --------------------------------------------------
# The old install served cloaked spam through two injected PHP endpoints. No
# rule is needed for them here: this is a static site with no PHP runtime, so
# every such request 404s on its own. (Cloudflare's _redirects supports only
# 3xx status codes, so a 410 Gone is not expressible here anyway.)
#
# Flushing those URLs out of the search index is handled deliberately, through
# the Search Console removals tool — see the launch checklist in the plan.
